check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0820537Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0829092Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0917862Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0926618Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0927256Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0927861Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0929424Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0929729Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0930275Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0930704Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0930947Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0931957Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0932255Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0932871Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0933785Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0934707Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0935770Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0936183Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0936519Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0936829Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0937372Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0938041Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0938307Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0938877Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0941015Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0942358Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0943010Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0943853Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0944017Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0944422Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0944811Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0945334Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0945954Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0946457Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0946903Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0947465Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0947953Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0948456Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0949422Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0949971Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0960050Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0960614Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0960919Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0961827Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0979318Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0979610Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0979990Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0988146Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0988810Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0989407Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0989623Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0989863Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0990148Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0990448Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0990954Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0991197Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0991337Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0991761Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0991995Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0992247Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0992692Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0992863Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0992907Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:33.0993467Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
