conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.2924936Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.2935205Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3040124Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3050249Z ^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3051112Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3051710Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3051972Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3052204Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3053450Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3054009Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3054391Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3055132Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3055473Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3056523Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3057491Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3058047Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3058436Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3058798Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3058997Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3059287Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3059502Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3059935Z    can use Nix.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3060093Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3060217Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3060392Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3060736Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3061266Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3063955Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3064169Z I will:
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3064552Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3064936Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3065740Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3066512Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3067249Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3067781Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3068310Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3068994Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3069438Z    /root
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3079672Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3080513Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3091925Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3092876Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3093393Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:49.3094570Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
