conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4111527Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4121633Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4226879Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4237829Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4238373Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4239116Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4239546Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4239941Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4240881Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4241439Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4241877Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4242905Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4243174Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4244223Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4244860Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4245356Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4245735Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4246060Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4246296Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4246574Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4246791Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4247317Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4247463Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4247594Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4247774Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4248069Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4248549Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4251309Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4251509Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4251852Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4252421Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4253441Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4254313Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4255009Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4255658Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4256477Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4257335Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4258169Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4267245Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4267852Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4280031Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4280972Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4281489Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4282214Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4283093Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4301649Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4302578Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4313296Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4314573Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4315377Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:05.4315773Z 
