conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1454779Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1455383Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1456209Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1457054Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1457330Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1457578Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1457996Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1458227Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1458683Z    can use Nix.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1458824Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1459046Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1459234Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1460154Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1460896Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1461633Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1462413Z I will:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1462786Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1464777Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1465604Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1466101Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1466911Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1467317Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1467690Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1468205Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1468640Z    /root
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1478016Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1478751Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1488641Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1489446Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1489766Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1490516Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1491176Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1509420Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1510357Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1519865Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1520826Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1521402Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1521620Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1521975Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1522317Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1522542Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1523001Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1523306Z 
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1523460Z If you would like to
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1523838Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-external (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:03.1524058Z 
