check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4696516Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4705907Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4706453Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4709508Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4709945Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4710226Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4711045Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4711438Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4711724Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4712227Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4712482Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4713428Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4714145Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4714749Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4715212Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4715618Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4715909Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4716257Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4716524Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4717014Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4717236Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4717395Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4717615Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4717995Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4718659Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4718966Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4719104Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4719399Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4719611Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4719962Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4720331Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4720680Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4721156Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4721400Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4721737Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4722133Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4734542Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4735186Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4745250Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4745890Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:06.4746127Z 
