conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4662075Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4750564Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4759153Z ^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4759688Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4760337Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4760668Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4760958Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4761639Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4762051Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4762322Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4762880Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4763153Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4763934Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4764413Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4764833Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4765167Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4765456Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4765673Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4765901Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4766136Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4766499Z    can use Nix.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4766639Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4766750Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4766915Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4767161Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4767575Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4770043Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4770250Z I will:
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4770563Z 
conformance-relock (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:53:58.4770842Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
