conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.3986007Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.3993255Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4077890Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4086765Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4087394Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4087974Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4088328Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4088684Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4089267Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4089621Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4090071Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4090966Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4091271Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4091757Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4092548Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4093372Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4093874Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4094135Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4094503Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4094886Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4095149Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4095707Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4096011Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4096209Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4096446Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4096933Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4097605Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4097919Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4098127Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4098516Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4098817Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4099328Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4100043Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4100620Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4101055Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4101570Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4102131Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4102658Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4110861Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4111579Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4122518Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4123177Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4126976Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4127612Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4128277Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4142427Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4151725Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4152754Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4153407Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4153927Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4154337Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4154584Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4154890Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4155117Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4155794Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4156072Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4156252Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4156638Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4157023Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4157339Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4157819Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4158026Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4158041Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.4158530Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
